          "text": "Here are reliable places in Singapore that offer full/\u201cexecutive\u201d health screening packages. I\u2019ve grouped them so you can scan quickly and pick what suits you.\n\nPublic hospitals (one-stop screening centres)\n- Singapore General Hospital \u2013 Health Assessment Centre (customised packages, coordinated same\u2011day tests). ([sgh.com.sg](https://www.sgh.com.sg/patient-care/specialties-services/Health-Assessment-Centre/pages/default.aspx?utm_source=openai))\n- National University Hospital \u2013 NUH Wellness Centre (customisable, evidence\u2011based screening; in\u2011house certified labs). ([nuh.com.sg](https://www.nuh.com.sg/care-at-nuh/health-screening/individual-health-screening?utm_source=openai))\n- Tan Tock Seng Hospital \u2013 Health Enrichment Centre (health screening with lifestyle advice; pre\u2011screen prep available). ([nhghealth.com.sg](https://www.nhghealth.com.sg/ttsh/patients-visitors/our-programmes/health-enrichment-centre?utm_source=openai))\n- Alexandra Hospital \u2013 WELL Programme (tailored screening services within a preventive\u2011care programme). ([ah.com.sg](https://www.ah.com.sg/our-services/well-programme?utm_source=openai))\n\nPrivate hospitals and dedicated executive screening centres\n- Parkway Shenton \u2013 Executive Health Screeners (centres at Mount Elizabeth/Gleneagles/Paragon/Republic Plaza; wide range including advanced options). ([parkwayshenton.com.sg](https://www.parkwayshenton.com.sg/services/health-screening?utm_source=openai))\n- Raffles Health Screeners \u2013 at Raffles Hospital (tiered packages such as Classic/Executive with add\u2011ons). ([raffleshealth.com](https://www.raffleshealth.com/enhanced-health-screening-packages/executive.html?utm_source=openai))\n- Farrer Park Hospital \u2013 HealthConnexion (comprehensive and cardiac\u2011focused screening; integrated with hospital services). ([farrerpark.com](https://www.farrerpark.com/Services/Health-Screening/About-HealthConnexion.html?utm_source=openai))\n- Fullerton Health \u2013 Executive Health Screening, incl. \u201cThe Signature Longevity & Wellness\u201d at Paragon. ([fullertonhealth.com](https://www.fullertonhealth.com/sg/services/executive-health-screening/?utm_source=openai))\n- Healthway Screening \u2013 flagship centres at OUE Downtown and Capitol (VIP and comprehensive packages). ([healthwayhealthscreening.com](https://www.healthwayhealthscreening.com/vip-screening?utm_source=openai))\n- Lifescan Medical & Wellness (SMG) \u2013 executive and cancer\u2011focused packages; Novena and Orchard locations. ([lifescanmedical.sg](https://lifescanmedical.sg/?utm_source=openai))\n- Minmed Group \u2013 clinic\u2011based packages islandwide; also home\u2011based screening if you prefer doing bloods at home. ([minmed.sg](https://minmed.sg/classic-health-screening/?utm_source=openai))\n- SATA CommHealth \u2013 community non\u2011profit provider with multi\u2011location screening (often good value). ([sata.com.sg](https://www.sata.com.sg/our-services/?utm_source=openai))\n\nIf you just want subsidised \u201cessentials\u201d\n- Healthier SG Screening (Screen for Life) subsidises core tests (e.g., diabetes, lipids, colorectal, cervical, breast cancer) for eligible Singapore Citizens at CHAS GP clinics/polyclinics. Useful if you only need the basics, not a full executive package. ([healthhub.sg](https://www.healthhub.sg/programmes/healthiersg-screening?utm_source=openai))\n\nHow to choose sensibly\n- Start with your age, sex, family history, and goals (e.g., \u201cbaseline check\u201d vs \u201cheart\u2011focused\u201d). Singapore\u2019s Screening Test Review Committee (STRC) advises using evidence\u2011based tests and avoiding unnecessary ones; most major centres above follow these guidelines. ([moh.gov.sg](https://www.moh.gov.sg/others/resources-and-statistics/strc-2026-volume-1/?utm_source=openai))\n\nWant me to shortlist 3\u20134 options and tell you what to book? Share:\n- your age/sex\n- any family history (heart disease, diabetes, cancers)\n- preferred location and weekday/Sat availability\n- rough budget range (e.g., <$300, $300\u2013$800, $800+)"
        }
